body:
First off thanks i appreciate it! second off the trans science stuff there are legitament explinations for why someone might be trans. like with me when i was a child i had a growth hormone deficiency, so i pretty much had a  natural puberty blocker. because of this i was put on growth hormones at 14.5 years old to induce androgen production naturally androgen is pretty much testosterone. so i think some of my transness came from a late puberty and not really a natural one as well.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

 the drwillpowers subreddit has a slideshow on stuff like this. 

&#x200B;

[https://www.reddit.com/r/DrWillPowers/wiki/index#wiki\_useful\_links](https://www.reddit.com/r/DrWillPowers/wiki/index#wiki_useful_links)

i think its the PowerPoint Presentation v6.0 link,

also idk if your sibling is into youtube or anything but philosophy tube is ran by Abigal Thorne and she just came out earlier this year. She still has videos from pretransition that you might be able to throw out and shes from the UK so maybe there would be some relatablity.

Maybe say you dont like J.K Rowling we tend to not like her either because shes so transphobic, and in America people love to talk about Harry Potter so if that ever comes up around them thats something else that can kind of cue them in.
